{{- /*
     ~/.local/bin/claude -> the system-wide caveman wrapper written by
     ansible/roles/claude_wrapper.

     ~/.local/bin is first on PATH, so whatever sits here is what `claude`
     means in a shell. Without this link it would be Claude Code's native
     launcher on Linux, and the Homebrew cask on macOS would also come
     before /usr/local/bin. Either way caveman would be bypassed. The
     wrapper recognises itself through the link and skips it when looking
     for the real binary.

     Replaces the old headroom wrapper. Like caveman, headroom points
     ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL at its own proxy, so stacking the two bypasses
     one of them. Each wrapper also exec'd the first *other* `claude` on
     PATH, so having both on PATH made them call each other in a loop.
     headroom was never installed on either machine; that wrapper was a
     pass-through.

     Claude Code's native updater rewrites this path when it updates. The
     next `chezmoi apply` restores the link.
*/ -}}
{{ if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}/usr/local/bin/claude{{ else }}/usr/bin/claude{{ end }}
